<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Elemental Shamans</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria our Hit cap is 15% and Spirit can be used towards it through <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=30674/elemental-precision">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_elementalprecision_1.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elemental Precision</span></a>. Expertise in MoP also contributes to our Hit cap. At 15% Hit, our spells will no longer be able to miss Raid bosses. This requires a total combined Spirit, Hit and Expertise of 5100. Normally we will have no Expertise, although we sometimes have a small amount of it from gems. Reaching Hit cap is very important for us because Hit rating is relatively cheap on gear relative to its damage contribution, and being Hit capped will also make our damage more reliable.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Gems for Elemental Shamans</span></h3>Gems can be a great place to grab any missing Hit, especially if we have many Blue Slots as <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76686/purified-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Purified Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Purified Imperial Amethyst</span></a> are the only good ways to utilize them. Because you are granted secondary stats at double the rate of Intellect, taking all socket bonuses is generally encouraged.<br/>
<br/>Once you're at 5100 Hit Rating or close, prioritize Intellect, while also picking up Haste in Yellow Sockets, and remember to Sim yourself for optimal outcomes once you reach a level of gear you will not easily replace.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76885/burning-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Burning Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Burning Primal Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c6">Red Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76694/brilliant-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Brilliant Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brilliant Primordial Ruby</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c11">Orange Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76668/reckless-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Reckless Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reckless Vermilion Onyx</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c9">Purple Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76686/purified-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Purified Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Purified Imperial Amethyst</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c3">Engineering Gems</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77542/quick-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Quick Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Quick Tinker's Gear</span></a> &amp; <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77546/sparkling-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Sparkling Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sparkling Tinker's Gear</span></a></div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Elemental Shamans</span></h2>Nearly every profession in Mists of Pandaria provides a similar boost to your characters damage output, but a few can be especially useful due to the way their boost is activated.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Elemental Shaman</h4>Engineering brings several gadgets and tools that can be helpful in your adventures. <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87215/wormhole-generator-pandaria">
<img alt="Wormhole Generator: Pandaria" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/sha_spell_fire_felfirenova.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wormhole Generator: Pandaria</span></a> will help you get around Pandaria quicker, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87214/blingtron-4000">
<img alt="Blingtron 4000" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_lilsmoky.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blingtron 4000</span></a> allowing you to repair from anywhere without having to go back to a town. In addition it provides the highest DPS boost out of any profession through <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126734/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_elementaloath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a>. And if all of that wasn't enough, it will provide a strong item for early gearing, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77537/energized-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Energized Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Energized Retinal Armor</span></a>. This item lets you choose your own secondary stats through the Cogwheel socket, letting you use cogwheels such as <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77542/quick-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Quick Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Quick Tinker's Gear</span></a> to make your perfect goggles!<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Elemental Shaman</h4>While you won't be equipping the things you craft with Tailoring, you will certainly benefit from <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=142173/lightweave-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweave Embroidery</span></a>, an embroidery unique to Tailors. The enchant will provide a chance to gain a large Intellect boost when casting spells. This is generally the highest DPS profession for casters, as you will be able to stack the proc with your cooldowns at the start of most fights.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="blacksmithing">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_blacksmithing.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Blacksmithing for Elemental Shaman</h4>Blacksmithing isn't a profession to choose in order to craft gear you would use, but rather for the benefits of two extra gem slots. Blacksmithing brings with it the now traditional additional Sockets with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55628/socket-bracer">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_socketedbracer.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Bracer</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55641/socket-gloves">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_addsocketglove.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Gloves</span></a>, giving a flexible stat choice that can be very strong. Especially with gems in Mists of Pandaria providing twice as much secondary stats, Blacksmithing can help you reach your secondary stat caps.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Elemental Shamans</span></h3>Crafted items are for the most part no longer restricted by profession, meaning that even if you aren't a Leatherworker, you can equip anything Leatherworkers craft. There are a few notable exceptions to this, the Engineer goggles and the Alchemist Trinket. There is also the Inscription Staff, which is bound to account.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79331/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a> is made through Inscription and will remain one of our best Trinket for a long time. As it is predicted be <b>extremely expensive</b>, players without a massive budget are advised to look at other uses for their gold early on in Mists of Pandaria.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85840/stormbreaker-chestguard">
<img alt="Stormbreaker Chestguard" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_mail_raidshaman_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stormbreaker Chestguard</span></a> is an item made with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a>. As it is an item with Crit that competes for the same spot as Tier pieces, it is not recommended to go for this one once we have access to Tier pieces from Celestial Dungeons.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85821/fists-of-lightning">
<img alt="Fists of Lightning" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_mail_raidshaman_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fists of Lightning</span></a> is an item made with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a>. It has a good distribution of secondary stats, it does however compete against Tier pieces which makes it hard to slot into our gear set once Celestial Dungeons are available.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77537/energized-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Energized Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Energized Retinal Armor</span></a> is exclusive to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=202/engineering">
<img alt="Engineering" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a>. You can choose your two preferred secondary stats for this item, making it always be a strong pick before Tier sets are available.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
